{:schema :historical-cascade-v1
 :id :s1-irc-stability-transport-context-cascade
 :problem
 {:id :s1-irc-transport-stability
  :statement "Drop-outs, duplicate messages, and re-connect races produce evidence gaps; a transport that silently drops messages is a transport that silently loses context."
  :source "futon5a/holes/stories/leaf-5.md:31-35 (survey witness runs/W1-witness-survey.md:37-51)"
  :solved-behaviour "The IRC server survives real-world conditions: server-initiated PING/PONG reaps zombie connections (F1), no reader thread blocks indefinitely (F2), no exception is silently discarded (F3), reconnecting clients reclaim their nick (F4), one stalled agent cannot block the relay (F5), and shutdown is coordinated (F6)."
  :scope "This record covers the six fixed failure modes of the IRC server adapter at mission closure (2026-02-23). It does not claim client-side reconnection, TLS, rate limiting, or federation, and it does not claim sustained operator-confirmed use without drop-outs, which the story scene sets as the closure bar (leaf-5.md:44-45)."
  :witness "futon3c/holes/missions/M-IRC-stability.md:302-310 (Completion, 2026-02-23: all 6 failure modes implemented, 16 stability tests)"}
 :source-pins
